      "message": "Good catch. This actually goes back to my uniforms proposal where I mentioned that the Metal codegen doesn\u0027t have consistent handling around descriptor sets. Metal doesn\u0027t support them, for uniforms we insist that declarations are all in the same set but for unsized arrays we did the flattening where (set\u003d1, binding\u003d0) gets assigned an implicit buffer index of 3? So graphite/ganesh need to know to call `setBuffer:offset:atIndex` on the appropriate encoder with this implicit index.\n\nI think the answer is to reject multiple \"set\" assignments in the metal backend instead of resorting to implicit assignments. If you agree, then I will fix the SkSL source for this shader to generate valid code and in a follow up introduce generalized enforcement around both descriptor set inconsistencies and binding overlaps.\n\nI filed skia:13664 (and actually ran into another can of worms when I started out on it). Let\u0027s fix this properly by implementing go/sksl-uniforms.",
